EXP 11 – JUNIT (ECLIPSE)

🔹 DO THIS
	1.	Open Eclipse
	2.	File → New → Java Project → Name: JUnitDemo
	3.	Right click src → New → Class → Name: Calculator
public class Calculator {
    public int add(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }
}
	4.	Right click project → Build Path → Add Library → JUnit → JUnit5 → Finish
	5.	Right click src → New → Class → Name: CalculatorTest
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;

public class CalculatorTest {
    Calculator calc = new Calculator();

    @Test
    public void testAdd() {
        assertEquals(5, calc.add(2, 3));
    }
}
	6.	Right click CalculatorTest.java → Run As → JUnit Test


